There is nothing stopping a bad actor from significantly adjusting their royalty after the primary sale.  This was mentioned during the discussions, and given careful consideration.  The decision was made that the onus was on the creator to get it right the first time.  If you are working in his space, and you want royalties, then you will ensure that its done correctly up front.  If you botch it, create a new policy and start again.  Testnet exists for this exact reason.  You can test everything there, before doing it in production.  There is nothing compelling about any of these arguments that would make me inclined to make a radical modification.  There is a reason that there were several people involved with the discussions.  There was multiple ways proposed, and the decision was made unanimously once the final design was settled on.

