@aleeusgr the "support any wallet" semantic wouldn't be an extension of CIP-0149 because
* the specification takes the delegation transaction (not an account transaction) as a means of determining who the wallet holder might support;
* generally wallet holders haven't sent a transaction directly to their dReps.

So as far as this CIP is concerned, the addresses receiving funds from the wallet and the designated address of the wallet's delegated dRep are generally in two separate sets.  It would be a completely non-overlapping specification to provide a means for the user to deliberately choose an arbitrary address in a wallet: a different CIP with a different specification & different goals.

